{"id":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"Deferrals","desc":"NO DEFERRALS (the human, 2026-08-22): a PR ships everything its item names and everything it spots in touched code; what cannot be done STOPS and ASKS. The Inbox holds only what the human chooses to park. ONE exception: a test found flaky on master that a PR does not own is NOT a deferral — it goes to the Inbox's top-level `flaky tests` ledger, governed by dag-pr-ci's FLAKE POLICY.","created":"2026-08-21T17:25:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:22:09-04:00"}
{"id":"flaky-tests","ord":"a7","title":"flaky tests — the ledger of tests found flaky on master that no PR owns","desc":"THE LEDGER, not the law: one entry per test file, sightings and dispositions as props on each entry. THE LAW lives in the boot chain — dag-pr-ci's FLAKE POLICY (filed here, dispatched immediately, pi or grok never Opus, one PR when several are open, auto-merge on green). The CI-runs doorbell and the orchestrator's own reading of run logs are the reporting channel (the claude-ci watcher seat retired on the human's ban, 2026-09-01); the orchestrator files what they surface.","created":"2026-08-22T11:51:06-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T20:18:25-04:00"}
{"id":"awaiting-word","ord":"a8","title":"Awaiting the human's word","desc":"The orchestrator's surfaced-but-unruled ledger, per orch-findings-inbox: each child names a proposal or observation and the word it awaits. Ruled children get their outcome written and are trashed or promoted to a lane.","created":"2026-08-29T11:40:15-04:00"}
{"id":"design-decisions","ord":"a9","title":"design decisions — agents' judgment calls awaiting the human's review","desc":"Choices agents made on their own, for your review — ONLY two kinds reach this queue (your ruling, 2026-08-29 20:15): (1) decisions with USER-FACING impact (what you see, how it behaves, where your data/config lives); (2) creation or non-creation of packages/*. Everything lower-level stays in the PR body's ## Design decisions section for reviewers and never lands here. One parent per PR, one child per qualifying choice, plain words. Reviewed: fine → trash; wrong → a lane to reverse it.","created":"2026-08-29T17:29:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T20:17:08-04:00"}
{"id":"await-queued-replay","parent":"awaiting-word","ord":"a3","title":"The adapter swallows the answer to a steered message","todo":true,"desc":"The human had to send \"Where's the PR…\" twice; three confirmed instances tonight, one shape: the text block written immediately after a message steered into a RUNNING turn reaches neither the panel nor the CLI's session store, while sibling blocks (tool calls, later text) survive.\\n\\nROOT CAUSE, traced 2026-09-02: agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp **PR #958** (\\\"settle a steered turn at idle, not at the interrupt\\\"), shipped in **v0.65.0**, carried into olai by **#456**'s 0.64.2→0.70.0 bump — pre-#456 olai predates #958 entirely, matching the human's no-bug memory. The PR's own text supplies the mechanism: steering is delivered at priority `now`, so the CLI ABORTS the running cycle (aborted partial output never finalizes into the jsonl — the storage half), and the adapter's new settle heuristic distinguishes cycles by watching for the injected message's replay, SWALLOWING output it attributes to the aborted cycle — the delivery half: an answer emitted right after the steer races the replay marker and is discarded. Evidence: session stamps (pre-#456 v2.1.220, current v2.1.232), store line 2152 (the steered send as a queued_command attachment), zero stored matches for three generated answers whose sibling blocks all stored.\\n\\nSecond, lesser defect: the queued_command attachment has no bubble on reopen (replay draws only messages) — likely predates #456.\\n\\nNEXT on the word: a minimal repro against the adapter's steering tests (#958 added four; none covers text-racing-the-replay), an upstream issue carrying it, and until the fix, the known workaround — answers to steered messages survive when emitted after the turn's next tool call rather than immediately.","created":"2026-09-02T08:14:15-04:00","changed":"2026-09-02T08:25:05-04:00","custom":{"node":"feat-chat"}}
{"id":"await-replay-misattribution","parent":"awaiting-word","ord":"a4","title":"A reopened chat wears your face on machine messages","todo":true,"desc":"Found by the human 2026-09-02 right after assigning this conversation to its node: a kolu doorbell message drew as THEIR tinted bubble, name and avatar. ROOT CAUSE: a plugin delivery goes out on the prompt lane, so the CLI's store records it as an ordinary user-role message; live delivery draws the machine presentation from olai core's own knowledge, but a REOPENED conversation rebuilds from the store — words, no mark (docs/chat.md documents this limit; the \"not by a person\" opening line is the designed mitigation) — and the speaker-naming feature then hangs the human's face on the user-role stretch. Any reopen does it; #471's assign gesture just made reopens routine. FIX HOME: olai core's replay — persist a machine-origin mark with plugin deliveries (the store already carries an origin field on queued sends) and honor it when rebuilding; the plugin face returns and the bubble goes left. A lane on the word.","created":"2026-09-02T10:39:33-04:00","custom":{"node":"feat-chat"}}
